import Json
import Optic
import Tagged
/-!
# Web.React

A React-style UI framework for Wiz: components, local state, typed event handlers,
keyed lists, a pure virtual DOM, deterministic server-side rendering (HTML strings),
and a keyed diff that produces small DOM patches. `web/framework/` has the browser
half (a patch applier and event delegation) and a demo.

The model is **VDOM, not fine-grained signals**, and it is chosen for the way the
existing web pages already work (web/Web.wiz, web/infoview.js):

* A page's state is a Wiz value held by JavaScript and handed back on every event
  (`wiz_web_step : state → event → state`). So the UI is a pure function
  `state → tree`, which is exactly what a virtual DOM wants. A signal graph would need
  a mutable heap, stable node identity and a subscription order that the step-function
  FFI does not have.
* The same `state → tree` function is the server-side renderer: `React.toHtml` is
  deterministic and needs no DOM, so `wiz doc` and the static pages can render a
  component tree without a browser.
* Keyed diffing is ~150 lines and has no runtime beyond the tree itself; a signal
  runtime (cells, dependency tracking, effect queue) would be larger in Wiz and would
  still need the diff for first paint.

Updates are **VDOM patches addressed by a child-index path** (`"0.2.1"`), through the
same `js_*` FFI the infoview uses: `React.patchesJson` gives JavaScript a list of
operations, and `web/framework/runtime.js` applies them. Nothing in this file is
`unsafe`, and no proof in it is evaluated natively (it trusts no native axiom).

## Components and local state

A component is a record of `init`, `update` and `view` (`React.Component`), with props
`P`, state `S` and messages `M`. Local state is addressed by a **lens**
(`lib/Optic.wiz`) into the application state: `useState` is `Lens.get`, `setState` is
`Lens.over`. Two components' lenses are disjoint paths, so their updates commute
(`Lens.Indep`), and the lens laws give read-after-write. This fits quantities: an
ordinary component's state is unrestricted data at ω.

A component that owns a **one-shot resource** (an in-flight request, a focus lease)
uses `React.Owned S`: a linear state cell (quantity 1). Every step takes the token and
must return it, so the kernel rejects using it twice and rejects dropping it on a
branch -- `React.Owned` is the `Uniq` pattern of `lib/Region.wiz` without regions.

```
import Optic
import Web.React

inductive Msg where
  | inc
  | dec

structure Model where
  count : Nat

def countL : Lens Model Nat := fun s => (s.count, fun n => Model.mk n)

def view (s : Model) : React.VNode Msg :=
  React.el "div" [React.class "counter"]
    [React.on "click" Msg.inc (React.el "button" List.nil [React.text "+"]),
     React.text "count: ", React.text (Nat.toString s.count)]   -- `import IO` for Nat.toString

def app : React.App Model Msg := React.App.mk (Model.mk 0)
  (fun m s => match m with
    | .inc => React.setState countL Nat.succ s
    | .dec => React.setState countL (fun n => Nat.sub n 1) s)
  view

#eval (React.App.render app (Model.mk 2)).html   -- the HTML string
```
-/

-- ## Nodes

/-- An HTML attribute: a name and a value. Both are escaped when rendered. -/
def React.Attr : Type := String × String
/-- An attribute, `React.attr "class" "pane"`. -/
def React.attr (name value : String) : React.Attr := (name, value)
/-- The `class` attribute. -/
def React.class (value : String) : React.Attr := React.attr "class" value
/-- The `id` attribute. -/
def React.id (value : String) : React.Attr := React.attr "id" value

/-- A virtual node, as a first-child/next-sibling forest (Wiz has no nested inductive
types, so children are a `children` chain and a node's `next` is its following
sibling). Build nodes with the smart constructors below, which take ordinary `List`s
and always end a chain at `.nil`.

`on event msg node` attaches a typed message to `node`'s DOM `event` (`click`, `input`,
`keydown`, …); `render` numbers handlers in document order and dispatch passes the
message to the app's `update`. `raw html` inserts `html` unescaped: it is the one trust
boundary (see `React.raw`). -/
inductive React.VNode (M : Type) where
  | nil
  | text (s : String) (next : React.VNode M)
  | raw (html : String) (next : React.VNode M)
  | el (tag : String) (key : String) (attrs : List React.Attr) (children : React.VNode M) (next : React.VNode M)
  | on (event : String) (msg : M) (body : React.VNode M) (next : React.VNode M)

/-- Put `rest` after the sibling chain `x`. -/
def React.append {M : Type} : React.VNode M → React.VNode M → React.VNode M
  | .nil, rest => rest
  | .text s n, rest => .text s (React.append n rest)
  | .raw h n, rest => .raw h (React.append n rest)
  | .el t k a cs n, rest => .el t k a cs (React.append n rest)
  | .on e m b n, rest => .on e m b (React.append n rest)

/-- `x` followed by the chain `rest`, merging two adjacent text nodes into one. HTML
merges adjacent text nodes when it parses a page, so the tree must merge them too: a
patch's child-index path addresses DOM nodes, and two text children would be one node
there. (Raw HTML is one element; see `React.raw`.) -/
def React.mergeText {M : Type} (x : React.VNode M) (rest : React.VNode M) : React.VNode M :=
  match x, rest with
  | .text a .nil, .text b r => .text (String.append a b) r
  | _, _ => React.append x rest

/-- A sibling chain from a list (adjacent text merged, as the DOM would). -/
def React.ofList {M : Type} : List (React.VNode M) → React.VNode M
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => React.mergeText x (React.ofList xs)

/-- A text node (escaped when rendered; a patch carries its unescaped text). -/
def React.text {M : Type} (s : String) : React.VNode M := .text s .nil
/-- Raw HTML, **not escaped**: only for output that is already trusted HTML (for
instance `TT.toHtml`, which escapes its own text). Every other text path escapes. -/
def React.raw {M : Type} (html : String) : React.VNode M := .raw html .nil
/-- An element: a tag, attributes and children. -/
def React.el {M : Type} (tag : String) (attrs : List React.Attr) (kids : List (React.VNode M)) : React.VNode M :=
  .el tag "" attrs (React.ofList kids) .nil
/-- A keyed element: its key is matched across renders when its siblings are reordered
(`React.diffChildren`). Only elements take keys; a key on anything else is ignored, and
keys must be unique among their siblings (a duplicate is matched to the first). -/
def React.keyed {M : Type} (key : String) (node : React.VNode M) : React.VNode M := match node with
  | .el t _ a cs n => .el t key a cs n
  | other => other
/-- Attach a message to a DOM event on `node`: one handler per event per element (the
last `on` for the same event wins, as in the DOM). -/
def React.on {M : Type} (event : String) (msg : M) (node : React.VNode M) : React.VNode M :=
  .on event msg node .nil
/-- A group of siblings, for a children list (do not use a group as one child). -/
def React.seq {M : Type} (kids : List (React.VNode M)) : React.VNode M := React.ofList kids

-- ## Rendering

/-- The rendered tree: text is raw (escaped when written out), attributes are strings,
and event handlers have become `data-wiz-on-EVENT="index"` attributes. -/
inductive React.RNode where
  | nil
  | text (s : String) (next : React.RNode)
  | raw (html : String) (next : React.RNode)
  | el (tag : String) (key : String) (attrs : List React.Attr) (children : React.RNode) (next : React.RNode)

/-- Put `rest` after the sibling chain `x`. -/
def React.RNode.append : React.RNode → React.RNode → React.RNode
  | .nil, rest => rest
  | .text s n, rest => .text s (React.RNode.append n rest)
  | .raw h n, rest => .raw h (React.RNode.append n rest)
  | .el t k a cs n, rest => .el t k a cs (React.RNode.append n rest)

/-- A sibling chain from a list. -/
def React.RNode.ofList : List React.RNode → React.RNode
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => React.RNode.append x (React.RNode.ofList xs)

/-- The siblings of a rendered node, detached (each with no `next`). -/
def React.RNode.siblings : React.RNode → List React.RNode
  | .nil => .nil
  | .text s n => .cons (.text s .nil) (React.RNode.siblings n)
  | .raw h n => .cons (.raw h .nil) (React.RNode.siblings n)
  | .el t k a cs n => .cons (.el t k a cs .nil) (React.RNode.siblings n)

/-- The key of a rendered node (empty for text, raw text and unkeyed elements). -/
def React.RNode.key : React.RNode → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .text _ _ => ""
  | .raw _ _ => ""
  | .el _ k _ _ _ => k

/-- The state of a render: the output (reversed characters), the number of the next
handler, and the handlers so far (reversed). -/
structure React.Out (M : Type) where
  acc : List Char
  next : Nat
  handlers : List (String × M)

/-- Whether `s` is in `xs`. -/
def React.member (s : String) : List String → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons x xs => match String.eq s x with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => React.member s xs

/-- Void HTML elements: no closing tag. -/
def React.void (tag : String) : Bool :=
  React.member tag (List.cons "area" (List.cons "base" (List.cons "br" (List.cons "col"
    (List.cons "embed" (List.cons "hr" (List.cons "img" (List.cons "input" (List.cons "link"
      (List.cons "meta" (List.cons "param" (List.cons "source" (List.cons "track"
        (List.cons "wbr" List.nil))))))))))))))

/-- The attribute name of a handler: one attribute per event, so an element can carry a
`click` and a `keydown` handler at once (`data-wiz-on-click="0"`). -/
def React.eventAttr (event : String) : String := String.append "data-wiz-on-" event

/-- The `data-wiz-on-EVENT` value of a handler: its index in the rendered handler table. -/
def React.eventValue (index : Nat) : String :=
  String.mk (Json.natChars index [])

/-- Attach the handler attribute for `event` (number `index`) to the head of `node`.
Nested `on`s put more attributes on the same element; a text node is wrapped in a
`span` so that it has somewhere to carry the attribute. -/
def React.attach {M : Type} (event : String) (index : Nat) : React.VNode M → React.VNode M
  | .el t k a cs n => .el t k (List.append a [(React.attr (React.eventAttr event) (React.eventValue index))]) cs n
  | .on e m b n => .on e m (React.attach event index b) n
  | .text s n => .el "span" "" [(React.attr (React.eventAttr event) (React.eventValue index))] (.text s .nil) n
  | .raw h n => .el "span" "" [(React.attr (React.eventAttr event) (React.eventValue index))] (.raw h .nil) n
  | .nil => .el "span" "" [(React.attr (React.eventAttr event) (React.eventValue index))] .nil .nil

/-- Turn a virtual tree into a rendered tree, numbering handlers in document order
(pre-order: the node's own handlers, then its children, then its next sibling). -/
partial def React.toR {M : Type} : React.VNode M → React.Out M → React.RNode × React.Out M
  | .nil, o => (.nil, o)
  | .text s n, o =>
    let r := React.toR n o;
    (.text s r.1, r.2)
  | .raw h n, o =>
    let r := React.toR n o;
    (.raw h r.1, r.2)
  | .el t k a cs n, o =>
    let rc := React.toR cs o;
    let rn := React.toR n rc.2;
    (.el t k a rc.1 rn.1, rn.2)
  | .on e m b n, o =>
    let index := o.next;
    let o1 : React.Out M := { o with next := index + 1, handlers := .cons (e, m) o.handlers };
    let r := React.toR (React.append (React.attach e index b) n) o1;
    (r.1, r.2)

/-- An attribute's HTML: ` name="value"`, escaped. -/
def React.attrHtml (a : React.Attr) (h : Html) : Html :=
  Html.lit "\"" (Html.lit (Tagged.esc a.2) (Html.lit "=\"" (Html.lit a.1 (Html.lit " " h))))

/-- Attributes' HTML, left to right. -/
def React.attrsHtml : List React.Attr → Html → Html
  | .nil, h => h
  | .cons a rest, h => React.attrsHtml rest (React.attrHtml a h)

/-- An opening tag, `<tag attrs>`, before `h`. -/
def React.openTag (tag : String) (attrs : List React.Attr) (h : Html) : Html :=
  Html.lit ">" (React.attrsHtml attrs (Html.lit tag (Html.lit "<" h)))

/-- A closing tag, `</tag>`, before `h`. -/
def React.closeTag (tag : String) (h : Html) : Html :=
  Html.lit ">" (Html.lit tag (Html.lit "</" h))

/-- A rendered node and its following siblings, as HTML, before `h`. -/
def React.renderRNode : React.RNode → Html → Html
  | .nil, h => h
  | .text s n, h => React.renderRNode n (Html.lit (Tagged.esc s) h)
  | .raw r n, h => React.renderRNode n (Html.lit r h)
  | .el t k a cs n, h =>
    let opened := React.openTag t a h;
    match React.void t with
    | .true => React.renderRNode n opened
    | .false => React.renderRNode n (React.closeTag t (React.renderRNode cs opened))

/-- A rendered tree as an HTML string. -/
def React.htmlOf (n : React.RNode) : String := match React.renderRNode n (Html.mk [] 0) with
  | .mk acc _ => String.mk (List.revOnto acc [])

/-- A rendered view: its tree (for diffing), its HTML, and its handler table
(`event, message`, in document order). -/
structure React.Rendered (M : Type) where
  tree : React.RNode
  html : String
  handlers : List (String × M)

/-- Render a virtual tree: HTML for SSR, handlers for dispatch, and the tree for a
later `React.Rendered.diff`. Deterministic: no clock, no hashing, no allocation order. -/
def React.render {M : Type} (v : React.VNode M) : React.Rendered M :=
  let o : React.Out M := React.Out.mk [] 0 [];
  let r := React.toR v o;
  React.Rendered.mk r.1 (React.htmlOf r.1) (List.revOnto r.2.handlers [])

/-- A virtual tree as an HTML string (SSR). -/
def React.toHtml {M : Type} (v : React.VNode M) : String := (React.render v).html

-- ## Patches

/-- A DOM update. Paths are child indices from the container (text nodes count too):
`"0"` is the first child, `"0.2"` its third child, `""` the container itself.
`insert` takes HTML for a new child; `move` removes the child at `src` and reinserts it
so that it ends up at index `dst`; `remove` removes at `index`. -/
inductive React.Patch where
  | replace (path : String) (html : String)
  | text (path : String) (s : String)
  | setAttr (path : String) (name : String) (value : String)
  | removeAttr (path : String) (name : String)
  | insert (path : String) (index : Nat) (html : String)
  | remove (path : String) (index : Nat)
  | move (path : String) (src : Nat) (dst : Nat)

/-- The element at `n`, if any. -/
partial def React.at {A : Type} (n : Nat) : List A → Option A
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => .some x
    | .false => React.at (n - 1) xs

/-- The element at `n`, or `d`. -/
partial def React.atD {A : Type} (d : A) (n : Nat) : List A → A
  | .nil => d
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => x
    | .false => React.atD d (n - 1) xs

/-- Insert `x` before position `n`. -/
partial def React.insertAt {A : Type} (n : Nat) (x : A) : List A → List A
  | .nil => .cons x .nil
  | .cons y ys => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => .cons x (.cons y ys)
    | .false => .cons y (React.insertAt (n - 1) x ys)

/-- Remove the element at `n`. -/
partial def React.removeAt {A : Type} (n : Nat) : List A → List A
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => xs
    | .false => .cons x (React.removeAt (n - 1) xs)

/-- Move the element at `src` so that it ends up at index `dst`. -/
def React.moveTo {A : Type} (src dst : Nat) (xs : List A) : List A :=
  match React.at src xs with
  | .some x => React.insertAt dst x (React.removeAt src xs)
  | .none => xs

/-- The key of the node; empty for text/raw. -/
def React.keyOf (n : React.RNode) : String := React.RNode.key n

/-- Whether the list has a key equal to `k`. -/
def React.hasKey (k : String) : List React.RNode → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons x xs => match String.eq (React.keyOf x) k with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => React.hasKey k xs

/-- The first index at or after `from` whose key is `k`. -/
partial def React.findKeyFrom (k : String) (from : Nat) : List React.RNode → Option Nat
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq from 0 with
    | .true => match String.eq (React.keyOf x) k with
      | .true => .some 0
      | .false => (match React.findKeyFrom k 0 xs with
        | .some n => .some (n + 1)
        | .none => .none)
    | .false => (match React.findKeyFrom k (from - 1) xs with
      | .some n => .some (n + 1)
      | .none => .none)

/-- Whether every node in the list is an element with a non-empty key. -/
def React.allKeyed : List React.RNode → Bool
  | .nil => .true
  | .cons x xs => match String.eq (React.keyOf x) "" with
    | .true => .false
    | .false => React.allKeyed xs

/-- Whether the parent is the root (whose child paths have no leading dot). -/
def React.childPath (parent : String) (i : Nat) : String :=
  match String.eq parent "" with
  | .true => String.mk (Json.natChars i [])
  | .false => String.mk (List.append (String.chars parent)
      (List.append (String.chars ".") (Json.natChars i [])))

/-- An attribute's value by name. -/
def React.attrValue (name : String) : List React.Attr → Option String
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons a rest => match String.eq a.1 name with
    | .true => .some a.2
    | .false => React.attrValue name rest

/-- Remove the attributes of `old` that `new` does not have. -/
def React.removedAttrs (path : String) : List React.Attr → List React.Attr → List React.Patch
  | .nil, _ => []
  | .cons a rest, new => match React.attrValue a.1 new with
    | .some _ => React.removedAttrs path rest new
    | .none => .cons (.removeAttr path a.1) (React.removedAttrs path rest new)

/-- Set the attributes of `new` that are absent from `old` or have another value. -/
def React.setAttrs (path : String) (old : List React.Attr) : List React.Attr → List React.Patch
  | .nil => []
  | .cons a rest => match React.attrValue a.1 old with
    | .some v => match String.eq v a.2 with
      | .true => React.setAttrs path old rest
      | .false => .cons (.setAttr path a.1 a.2) (React.setAttrs path old rest)
    | .none => .cons (.setAttr path a.1 a.2) (React.setAttrs path old rest)

/-- Patches for the attributes: remove the ones that went away, set the new or changed
ones. -/
def React.diffAttrs (path : String) (old new : List React.Attr) : List React.Patch :=
  List.append (React.removedAttrs path old new) (React.setAttrs path old new)

-- (diffNode and diffChildren are mutual: an element's children are diffed by the same
-- function that diffs nodes.)

mutual
/-- Patches turning the node `old` into `new` at `path` (both are single nodes). -/
partial def React.diffNode (path : String) (old : React.RNode) (new : React.RNode) : List React.Patch :=
  match old, new with
  | .nil, .nil => []
  | .text s _, .text s' _ => match String.eq s s' with
    | .true => []
    | .false => [(.text path s')]
  | .raw h _, .raw h' _ => match String.eq h h' with
    | .true => []
    | .false => [(.replace path h')]
  | .el t k a cs _, .el t' k' a' cs' _ =>
    match String.eq t t' with
    | .false => [(.replace path (React.htmlOf new))]
    | .true => match String.eq k k' with
      | .false => [(.replace path (React.htmlOf new))]
      | .true => List.append (React.diffAttrs path a a')
          (React.diffChildren path (React.RNode.siblings cs) (React.RNode.siblings cs'))
  | _, _ => [(.replace path (React.htmlOf new))]

/-- Patches for a children list at `base` (which ends with `.`, or is empty at the
root): keyed when both lists are fully keyed, positional otherwise. -/
partial def React.diffChildren (base : String) (old new : List React.RNode) : List React.Patch :=
  match React.allKeyed old with
  | .true => match React.allKeyed new with
    | .true => React.diffKeyed base old new
    | .false => React.diffPositional base 0 old new
  | .false => React.diffPositional base 0 old new

/-- Positional diff: pair by index, then insert or remove at the tail. -/
partial def React.diffPositional (base : String) (i : Nat) : List React.RNode → List React.RNode → List React.Patch
  | .nil, .nil => []
  | .nil, .cons n ns =>
    .cons (.insert base i (React.htmlOf n)) (React.diffPositional base (i + 1) [] ns)
  | .cons o os, .nil =>
    .cons (.remove base i) (React.diffPositional base i os [])
  | .cons o os, .cons n ns =>
    List.append (React.diffNode (React.childPath base i) o n)
      (React.diffPositional base (i + 1) os ns)

/-- Keyed diff: drop the old children that are gone, then walk the new list, moving a
matching child into place (or inserting it), and finally remove the leftovers. -/
partial def React.diffKeyed (base : String) (old new : List React.RNode) : List React.Patch :=
  let kept := React.dropMissing base new 0 old;
  let walked := React.keyedLoop base 0 kept.1 new [];
  List.append kept.2 walked.2

/-- The old children still present in `new`, with `remove` patches for the others.
`j` is the child's current index (the number kept so far). -/
def React.dropMissing (base : String) (new : List React.RNode) (j : Nat) :
    List React.RNode → List React.RNode × List React.Patch
  | .nil => ([], [])
  | .cons o os =>
    match React.hasKey (React.keyOf o) new with
    | .true => let rest := React.dropMissing base new (j + 1) os; (.cons o rest.1, rest.2)
    | .false => let rest := React.dropMissing base new j os;
      (rest.1, .cons (.remove base j) rest.2)

/-- Walk `new` at index `i` over the current list `cur`, producing patches. -/
partial def React.keyedLoop (base : String) (i : Nat) (cur : List React.RNode) :
    List React.RNode → List React.Patch → List React.RNode × List React.Patch
  | .nil, acc => (cur, List.append acc (React.removeTail base i (List.length cur - i)))
  | .cons n ns, acc =>
    match React.at i cur with
    | .some c => match String.eq (React.keyOf c) (React.keyOf n) with
      | .true => React.keyedLoop base (i + 1) cur ns
          (List.append acc (React.diffNode (React.childPath base i) c n))
      | .false => match React.findKeyFrom (React.keyOf n) (i + 1) cur with
        | .some j => React.keyedLoop base (i + 1) (React.moveTo j i cur) ns
            (List.append acc (.cons (.move base j i)
              (React.diffNode (React.childPath base i) (React.atD n j cur) n)))
        | .none => React.keyedLoop base (i + 1) (React.insertAt i n cur) ns
            (List.append acc [(.insert base i (React.htmlOf n))])
    | .none => React.keyedLoop base (i + 1) (React.insertAt i n cur) ns
        (List.append acc [(.insert base i (React.htmlOf n))])

/-- Remove `k` children at index `i` (each removal shifts the next into place). -/
def React.removeTail (base : String) (i : Nat) : Nat → List React.Patch
  | .zero => []
  | .succ k => .cons (.remove base i) (React.removeTail base i k)
end

/-- Patches from one rendered view to another. -/
def React.Rendered.diff {M : Type} (old new : React.Rendered M) : List React.Patch :=
  React.diffChildren "" (React.RNode.siblings old.tree) (React.RNode.siblings new.tree)

-- ## JSON, for the browser half

/-- `map`, locally (the framework does not import lib/Text.wiz). -/
def React.map {A B : Type} (f : A → B) : List A → List B
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => .cons (f x) (React.map f xs)

/-- One patch as JSON (`web/framework/runtime.js` applies it). -/
def React.Patch.toJson (p : React.Patch) : Json := match p with
  | .replace path html => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "replace"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "html" (Json.mkStr html)) List.nil)))
  | .text path s => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "text"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "text" (Json.mkStr s)) List.nil)))
  | .setAttr path name value => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "setAttr"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "name" (Json.mkStr name))
        (.cons (Json.field "value" (Json.mkStr value)) List.nil))))
  | .removeAttr path name => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "removeAttr"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "name" (Json.mkStr name)) List.nil)))
  | .insert path index html => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "insert"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "index" (Json.ofNat index))
        (.cons (Json.field "html" (Json.mkStr html)) List.nil))))
  | .remove path index => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "remove"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "index" (Json.ofNat index)) List.nil)))
  | .move path src dst => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "move"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "src" (Json.ofNat src))
        (.cons (Json.field "dst" (Json.ofNat dst)) List.nil))))

/-- A patch list as JSON, for `js_patch`. -/
def React.patchesJson (ps : List React.Patch) : String :=
  Json.render (Json.mkArr (React.map React.Patch.toJson ps))

-- ## Components, state, dispatch

/-- Read a component's local state: `useState` is a lens's get. -/
def React.useState {S A : Type} (l : Lens S A) (s : S) : A := Lens.get l s
/-- Update a component's local state: `setState` is a lens's over. The lens laws
(`Lens.GetPut`, `Lens.PutGet`) give read-after-write; two components' lenses on
independent paths commute (`Lens.Indep`). -/
def React.setState {S A : Type} (l : Lens S A) (f : A → A) (s : S) : S := Lens.over l f s
/-- A reducer on a component's local state (`useReducer`). -/
def React.useReducer {S A M : Type} (l : Lens S A) (step : M → A → A) (m : M) (s : S) : S :=
  Lens.over l (step m) s

/-- A component: its initial state from props, its update, and its view. -/
structure React.Component (P S M : Type) where
  init : P → S
  update : M → S → S
  view : P → S → React.VNode M

/-- Render a component (`props`, `state`) to a `Rendered`. -/
def React.Component.render {P S M : Type} (c : React.Component P S M) (p : P) (s : S) : React.Rendered M :=
  React.render (c.view p s)

/-- A whole app: initial state, update and view. -/
structure React.App (S M : Type) where
  init : S
  update : M → S → S
  view : S → React.VNode M

/-- The app's view at `s`, rendered. -/
def React.App.render {S M : Type} (a : React.App S M) (s : S) : React.Rendered M :=
  React.render (a.view s)

/-- SSR: the app at `s` as HTML. -/
def React.App.html {S M : Type} (a : React.App S M) (s : S) : String := (React.App.render a s).html

/-- The message of handler `i` (document order), if any. -/
partial def React.handlerAt {M : Type} (i : Nat) : List (String × M) → Option M
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons h hs => match Nat.beq i 0 with
    | .true => .some h.2
    | .false => React.handlerAt (i - 1) hs

/-- Dispatch handler `i` (the browser sends its `data-wiz-on-EVENT` index): the next state. -/
def React.App.dispatch {S M : Type} (a : React.App S M) (s : S) (i : Nat) : S :=
  match React.handlerAt i (React.App.render a s).handlers with
  | .some m => a.update m s
  | .none => s

/-- Dispatch only if the handler's event name is `event` (the browser sends both, so a
stale index from a previous render cannot fire the wrong message). -/
def React.App.event {S M : Type} (a : React.App S M) (s : S) (event : String) (i : Nat) : S :=
  match React.at i (React.App.render a s).handlers with
  | .some h => match String.eq h.1 event with
    | .true => a.update h.2 s
    | .false => s
  | .none => s

/-- The patches from the app's state `s` to `s'` (render both, keyed-diff). -/
def React.App.patch {S M : Type} (a : React.App S M) (s s' : S) : List React.Patch :=
  React.Rendered.diff (React.App.render a s) (React.App.render a s')

/-- `React.App.patch` as JSON, for `js_patch`. -/
def React.App.patches {S M : Type} (a : React.App S M) (s s' : S) : String :=
  React.patchesJson (React.App.patch a s s')

-- ## Owned (linear) state

/-- A one-shot state cell: the token is used at quantity 1, so the kernel rejects
using it twice and rejects dropping it. The state itself is ordinary (ω) data, as in
`Uniq`. Only this module constructs it (`private mk`). -/
inductive React.Owned (S : Type) where
  | private mk (state : S)

/-- A new one-shot cell. -/
def React.Owned.new {S : Type} (s : S) : React.Owned S := React.Owned.mk s

/-- Use the cell once: run `k` on the state and return its result. -/
def React.Owned.read {S B : Type} (1 o : React.Owned S) (k : S → B) : B :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => k s

/-- The state, and the cell back (`*o` in direct style). -/
def React.Owned.peek {S : Type} (1 o : React.Owned S) : S × React.Owned S :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => (s, React.Owned.mk s)

/-- Update the state, giving the cell back. -/
def React.Owned.update {S : Type} (1 o : React.Owned S) (f : S → S) : React.Owned S :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => React.Owned.mk (f s)

/-- Replace the state, giving the cell back. -/
def React.Owned.set {S : Type} (1 o : React.Owned S) (s : S) : React.Owned S :=
  match o with
  | .mk _ => React.Owned.mk s

/-- End the one-shot state: its final value (the only way to discard the cell, and it
must be written on every path). -/
def React.Owned.end {S : Type} (1 o : React.Owned S) : S :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => s

attribute [inline] React.Owned.new
attribute [inline] React.Owned.read
attribute [inline] React.Owned.peek
attribute [inline] React.Owned.update
attribute [inline] React.Owned.set
attribute [inline] React.Owned.end
